WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.520
You can have your own Jarvis:

2
00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:03.040
an assistant that talks to you through

3
00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:04.900
Telegram, remembers your conversations, and has the

4
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:06.300
personality you choose.

5
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.680
This is sequence two,

6
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:08.420
INTELECTO.

7
00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:09.980
In this video: what it is,

8
00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:11.000
how it thinks,

9
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.500
how to install it, and at the end,

10
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:13.780
what it becomes when you connect

11
00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:14.800
the next sequences.

12
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:16.540
INTELECTO is a personal assistant written

13
00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:17.600
from scratch in Python.

14
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:18.900
No heavy framework,

15
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.540
no Docker, no web panel.

16
00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:22.240
It's about three thousand lines and

17
00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:23.060
seven dependencies.

18
00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.160
Small on purpose:

19
00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:25.160
you can read it,

20
00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:26.420
understand it, and change it.

21
00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:27.660
The path is simple.

22
00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.240
You send a message on Telegram.

23
00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:30.640
INTELECTO receives it,

24
00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:31.820
the agent loop thinks,

25
00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:33.020
searches the memory,

26
00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:35.100
uses tools, and the model generates the

27
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:36.580
answer: in the cloud,

28
00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:38.320
through OpenRouter, or locally,

29
00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:39.200
through Ollama.

30
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.120
The answer comes back on Telegram.

31
00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:43.140
It's the same design as the big assistants,

32
00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:43.940
only it's yours.

33
00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:45.860
Installation starts with one command:

34
00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:47.520
start dot sh.

35
00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:49.760
It sets up the environment and opens a

36
00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:52.040
six-step setup assistant.

37
00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:53.660
You create the bot on Telegram with

38
00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:55.300
BotFather and paste the token.

39
00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:56.300
You choose the model.

40
00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:57.960
You set the name and the personality.

41
00:00:57.960 --> 00:00:59.880
And your bot starts answering.

42
00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:01.420
What makes it a Jarvis is

43
00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:03.100
the memory and the personality.

44
00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:04.740
It remembers what you talked about,

45
00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:05.640
keeps what matters,

46
00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:07.500
and speaks the way you defined.

47
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.940
It's not a website that forgets everything

48
00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:10.160
when you close the tab.

49
00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:11.940
That's why it comes after OSWork.

50
00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:13.320
You'll need a terminal,

51
00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.360
folders, a configuration file, and a

52
00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:16.900
key stored in the right place.

53
00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:18.660
If you did sequence one, you'll install

54
00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:19.740
Jarvis without a scare.

55
00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:21.580
And the next step is to give it real

56
00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:22.520
work to do:

57
00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:23.420
task queues,

58
00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:24.220
in sequence three.

59
00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:26.420
INTELECTO, the installation guide, and

60
00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:28.160
the Jarvis area are on INEMA dot

61
00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:30.080
CLUB, open and free.

62
00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:30.960
Install yours,

63
00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:31.660
give it a name,

64
00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:33.040
and start talking.
